  "note": "Election of the whole council (21 members, seven for each of the Central, East and West wards) on 15 January 1923. All 21 seats were filled without a contest (Belfast News-Letter, 10 and 13 January 1923). Robert Hamill and W. R. Kerr, the retiring councillors renominated, withdrew; Peter M'Shane and Robert J. Cardwell were selected to fill the vacancies. Returned unopposed.",
  "correctionNote": "Citation corrected from the page images (w8-review, Nov 2026): the withdrawals are reported in the Irish News, 10 January 1923, p. 6 (the News-Letter page cited before does not exist), and the East Ward nominations in the Belfast News-Letter and the Northern Whig of 6 January 1923; the Whig prints Robert Andrey and the News-Letter Robert Ardis (the 1926 return has R. Ardrey), so the name is kept as the Whig prints it until a third source settles it."
